Subject: [PATCH] arm64: Surface Laptop 7 QSPI touchpad support on Ubuntu 7.3

Port the QSPI/GPI and HID-over-SPI v3 implementation from ELLX commit
0e9944fa4cf2ccf575f5162bfd53ed4dc1592251 to Ubuntu linux 7.3.0-5.5
(upstream v7.3-rc3). Enable the touchpad wiring only for
microsoft,romulus15.

Retain the new geni_spi_desc resource/clock/power callbacks and SA8255P
match entry. Extend that descriptor with the QSPI flag instead of adding
a second match-data structure. Use the new scoped runtime-PM acquisition
on error returns; do not reintroduce the old manual PM cleanup label.

Adapt the HID transport to in-tree Kbuild and drain all asynchronous
workers on removal before freeing buffers. Firmware protocol and board
power sequencing follow the community implementation. Camera, audio and
unrelated ELLX changes are excluded.

The Ubuntu 7.2 version of this patch was retired on 2026-09-27; the DMA,
HID transport and Romulus15 wiring portions were identical in both.

Origin: ELLX commit 0e9944fa4cf2ccf575f5162bfd53ed4dc1592251
https://github.com/ProgrammerIn-wonderland/ELLX-Kernel
